      "properties": {
        "preconditions": {
          "text": "The transferFrom function is invoked, moving tokens from an owner (from) on behalf of a spender (msg.sender).; Off-chain tooling (block explorers, wallets, indexing services, accounting) reconstructs senders and balances from Transfer(from,to,amount) events.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "and",
            "args": [
              {
                "var": "c05007057_transferfrom_invoked"
              },
              {
                "var": "c05007057_offchain_reconstructs_from_events"
              }
            ]
          },
          "derivation": "Program conjunction of selected report preconditions.",
          "source_ids": [
            "p_transferfrom_invoked",
            "p_event_consumed_offchain"
          ],
          "evidence": [
            "The `transferFrom` function emits the `Transfer` event with the wrong sender address.",
            "Instead of reporting the actual owner whose tokens are being moved, the event reports msg.sender (the spender calling `transferFrom`).",
            "In ``TokenWrapper.sol`` the ``transferFrom`` implementation emits the ERC-20 ``Transfer`` event with ``msg.sender`` as the ``from`` address:",
            "- __Off-chain tooling breaks:__ Block explorers, wallets, indexing services, event-driven accounting, and analytics assume ``Transfer(from,to,amount)`` corresponds to the actual sender. When the event reports ``msg.sender`` (the spender) instead of ``from`` (the token owner), these tools will record incorrect senders and balances."
          ]
        },
        "safety": {
          "text": "When transferFrom moves an owner's tokens, the emitted Transfer event's from address should equal the from parameter (the token owner), per the ERC-20 event convention.",
          "expression": {
